<% content_for :title, "On the Inside | Bipolar Sober" %>

<main class="perspectives-inside-page">

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="perspectives-inside-hero">

    <div class="perspectives-inside-hero-content">

      <p class="perspectives-inside-eyebrow">
        BIPOLAR SOBER / PERSPECTIVES / ON THE INSIDE
      </p>

      <h1>
        <span>ON THE</span>
        <span>FUCKING</span>
        <span>INSIDE.</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="perspectives-inside-intro">
        JAIL JOURNALS.<br>
        WHAT HAPPENED. WHAT I WROTE.<br>
        WHAT I DON'T WANT TO FORGET.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- INTRO -->
  <section class="pi-section pi-section-black">

    <p class="pi-number">01 / ON THE INSIDE</p>

    <h2>
      I WROTE<br>
      IT DOWN.
    </h2>

    <div class="pi-copy">

      <p>
        These are pieces of my journals from jail.
      </p>

      <p>
        Not the cleaned-up version. Not the version where everything
        gets turned into a neat recovery lesson after the fact.
      </p>

      <p>
        These are the things I noticed when I was actually there:
        the waiting, the noise, the boredom, the routines,
        the loss of privacy, the people, the thoughts,
        and the strange little details that suddenly became
        my entire fucking world.
      </p>

      <p>
        Some of it makes more sense to me now.
        Some of it still doesn't.
      </p>

      <div class="pi-callout">
        THIS ISN'T WHAT I THINK<br>
        JAIL WAS LIKE.<br><br>
        THIS IS WHAT I WROTE<br>
        WHILE I WAS FUCKING THERE.
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- TWO PERSPECTIVES -->
  <section class="pi-section pi-section-pink">

    <p class="pi-number">02 / THEN + NOW</p>

    <h2>
      TWO VERSIONS<br>
      OF THE SAME<br>
      STORY.
    </h2>

    <div class="pi-copy">

      <p>
        There are really two voices in these pages.
      </p>

      <div class="pi-two-column">

        <div class="pi-perspective-card">
          <span>THEN</span>

          <h3>
            ME ON<br>
            THE INSIDE.
          </h3>

          <p>
            What I was thinking while it was happening.
            Angry. Bored. Scared. Irritated. Restless.
            Observant. Sometimes numb. Sometimes completely
            overwhelmed by shit that would normally seem tiny.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="pi-perspective-card">
          <span>NOW</span>

          <h3>
            ME LOOKING<br>
            BACK.
          </h3>

          <p>
            What I notice now that I'm outside of it.
            Patterns I couldn't see. Things I understand differently.
            Things I still disagree with. Things I never want
            to experience again.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <p>
        I don't want the person I am now to rewrite the person
        who actually lived it.
      </p>

      <p>
        Both perspectives belong here.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- THE DETAILS -->
  <section class="pi-section pi-section-yellow">

    <p class="pi-number">03 / THE LITTLE SHIT</p>

    <h2>
      YOUR WORLD<br>
      GETS REALLY<br>
      FUCKING SMALL.
    </h2>

    <div class="pi-copy">

      <p>
        When most of your normal life disappears, little things
        become enormous.
      </p>

      <div class="pi-fragments">

        <span>THE CLOCK.</span>
        <span>THE DOOR.</span>
        <span>THE LIGHTS.</span>
        <span>THE FOOD.</span>
        <span>THE NOISE.</span>
        <span>THE BED.</span>
        <span>THE PHONE.</span>
        <span>THE WAITING.</span>
        <span>THE COUNT.</span>
        <span>THE NEXT FUCKING HOUR.</span>

      </div>

      <p>
        That's one reason I want the details here.
      </p>

      <p>
        Memory likes to compress an experience into a sentence:
        <strong>"I was in jail."</strong>
      </p>

      <p>
        A journal doesn't let it disappear that easily.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- WAITING -->
  <section class="pi-section pi-section-purple">

    <p class="pi-number">04 / WAITING</p>

    <h2>
      WAIT.<br>
      THEN WAIT<br>
      SOME MORE.
    </h2>

    <div class="pi-copy">

      <p>
        Waiting became its own activity.
      </p>

      <p>
        Waiting for food.
        Waiting for a door.
        Waiting for information.
        Waiting for somebody to answer a question.
        Waiting to make a call.
        Waiting for the next part of the day.
      </p>

      <p>
        When you don't control the schedule, time feels different.
      </p>

      <div class="pi-callout">
        YOU'RE NOT DECIDING<br>
        WHAT HAPPENS NEXT.<br><br>
        YOU'RE WAITING TO FIND OUT.
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- FREEDOM -->
  <section class="pi-section pi-section-black">

    <p class="pi-number">05 / FREEDOM</p>

    <h2>
      YOU NOTICE IT<br>
      WHEN IT'S<br>
      FUCKING GONE.
    </h2>

    <div class="pi-copy">

      <p>
        Freedom usually doesn't feel dramatic when you have it.
      </p>

      <p>
        You open a door.
        You make food.
        You go outside.
        You take a shower.
        You turn off a light.
        You call somebody.
        You decide you're tired and go to bed.
      </p>

      <p>
        They're ordinary choices.
      </p>

      <p>
        Until they aren't yours anymore.
      </p>

      <div class="pi-thought">
        I DIDN'T UNDERSTAND HOW MANY TINY FREEDOMS
        MADE UP MY LIFE UNTIL SOMEBODY ELSE CONTROLLED THEM.
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- THE JOURNALS -->
  <section class="pi-journals">

    <div class="pi-journals-heading">

      <p>06 / FROM THE JOURNALS</p>

      <h2>
        THE SHIT<br>
        I ACTUALLY<br>
        WROTE.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Pieces from the journals, organized by what was happening
        and what was going through my head.
      </p>

    </div>


    <div class="pi-journal-grid">

      <article class="pi-journal-card pi-card-pink">

        <p class="pi-card-number">01</p>

        <h3>
          THE FIRST<br>
          HOURS
        </h3>

        <p>
          Arrival. Processing. Confusion. Realizing where I was
          and that I wasn't leaving whenever I wanted.
        </p>

        <span>JOURNAL ENTRY →</span>

      </article>


      <article class="pi-journal-card pi-card-yellow">

        <p class="pi-card-number">02</p>

        <h3>
          THE<br>
          WAITING
        </h3>

        <p>
          What happens to your brain when there is almost nothing
          to do except wait for the next thing to happen.
        </p>

        <span>JOURNAL ENTRY →</span>

      </article>


      <article class="pi-journal-card pi-card-purple">

        <p class="pi-card-number">03</p>

        <h3>
          THE<br>
          PEOPLE
        </h3>

        <p>
          The people around me, the conversations, the personalities,
          and what happens when strangers suddenly share a tiny world.
        </p>

        <span>JOURNAL ENTRY →</span>

      </article>


      <article class="pi-journal-card pi-card-black">

        <p class="pi-card-number">04</p>

        <h3>
          THE LITTLE<br>
          THINGS
        </h3>

        <p>
          Food. Sleep. Noise. Clothes. Phones. Showers.
          Doors. Rules. All the shit you normally never think about.
        </p>

        <span>JOURNAL ENTRY →</span>

      </article>


      <article class="pi-journal-card pi-card-yellow">

        <p class="pi-card-number">05</p>

        <h3>
          INSIDE<br>
          MY HEAD
        </h3>

        <p>
          Fear, anger, boredom, regret, mental health,
          addiction, and whatever else my brain decided
          to throw at me while I couldn't leave.
        </p>

        <span>JOURNAL ENTRY →</span>

      </article>


      <article class="pi-journal-card pi-card-pink">

        <p class="pi-card-number">06</p>

        <h3>
          LOOKING<br>
          BACK
        </h3>

        <p>
          What I see differently now — and what I absolutely
          fucking don't.
        </p>

        <span>REFLECTION →</span>

      </article>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- WHY KEEP IT -->
  <section class="pi-section pi-section-yellow">

    <p class="pi-number">07 / WHY KEEP THIS?</p>

    <h2>
      BECAUSE MEMORY<br>
      IS A FUCKING<br>
      LIAR.
    </h2>

    <div class="pi-copy">

      <p>
        Time softens things.
      </p>

      <p>
        That's useful sometimes.
      </p>

      <p>
        It's also dangerous when my brain starts editing out
        the parts of the story that are inconvenient.
      </p>

      <p>
        Especially when addiction starts negotiating.
      </p>

      <div class="pi-thought">
        "IT WASN'T THAT BAD."
      </div>

      <p>
        Yeah.
      </p>

      <p>
        That's exactly why I fucking wrote it down.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- NOT A MORAL -->
  <section class="pi-section pi-section-pink">

    <p class="pi-number">08 / NOT A MORAL</p>

    <h2>
      I'M NOT HERE<br>
      TO TURN IT<br>
      INTO A FABLE.
    </h2>

    <div class="pi-copy">

      <p>
        I don't need every shitty thing that's happened to me
        to secretly be a beautiful gift.
      </p>

      <p>
        Some experiences suck.
      </p>

      <p>
        I can learn from something without becoming grateful
        that it happened.
      </p>

      <p>
        I can change because of something without pretending
        the thing itself was good.
      </p>

      <div class="pi-callout">
        SOMETIMES THE LESSON ISN'T<br>
        "EVERYTHING HAPPENS FOR A REASON."<br><br>
        SOMETIMES IT'S<br>
        "I DON'T WANT TO FUCKING GO BACK."
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- ENDING -->
  <section class="pi-ending">

    <p>
      I WAS THERE.<br>
      I WROTE IT DOWN.<br>
      I GOT OUT.
    </p>

    <h2>
      DON'T<br>
      FUCKING<br>
      FORGET.
    </h2>

    <p class="pi-ending-copy">
      The journals stay because the person who wrote them
      deserves to be remembered accurately.
    </p>

    <%= link_to "← BACK TO PERSPECTIVES",
        perspectives_path,
        class: "pi-back-link" %>

  </section>

</main>